Wait, but the EOCD record is at the end of the file (or at least after the EOCD64 locator). The EOCD64 record is before the EOCD64 locator. So the EOCD record is after the EOCD64 record. The check `cd->offset + cd->size > buf_offset + eocd_offset` (where `eocd_offset` is the offset of the EOCD record) allows the central directory to extend up to the EOCD record, which is after the EOCD64 record.

